# etymd content-screen exceptions — ONE FILE, one labeled line per field.
# A `pattern` line opens a record (the pattern is the rest of the line, verbatim — any
# characters, no escaping); `reason`, `date`, `author` lines complete it. A bare pattern
# line is a self-name exemption (the repo naming itself) and needs no provenance.
# This file exempts strings the TOOL'S OWN CODE and tests must contain: a scanner
# necessarily carries the patterns it screens for.

